Speaker 0: I'd say it was 80% the same people I work with at East to the point that we didn't even have a meeting of like, who does what?

531
00:45:51,705 --> 00:45:56,229
Speaker 0: we all just walked in and kind of went to their, went to the place we thought was right and just ran it.

532
00:45:56,269 --> 00:46:00,691
Speaker 0: Like, we didn't really need, like we didn't have to plan anything because it was all like 10 year veterans.

533
00:46:02,254 --> 00:46:03,777
Speaker 0: But that's, that's unsustainable.

534
00:46:03,817 --> 00:46:07,825
Speaker 0: We need more enforcers.

535
00:46:08,707 --> 00:46:13,043
Speaker 0: The main events was actually interesting because for the first time packs unplugged had concerts.

536
00:46:13,666 --> 00:46:15,777
Speaker 0: And I remember thinking, what concerts would they put there?

537
00:46:15,797 --> 00:46:16,802
Speaker 0: I could think of a few things.

538
00:46:17,305 --> 00:46:21,182
Speaker 0: It was the old packs, West standby, Jonathan Colton, Paul and storm.

539
00:46:21,222 --> 00:46:21,704
Speaker 0: And you know what?

540
00:46:22,427 --> 00:46:26,497
Speaker 0: To their credit, they kept like they filled that room.

541
00:46:27,360 --> 00:46:32,134
Speaker 0: And I would say only about a fifth of the people in that room had any idea who the hell they were.

542
00:46:33,136 --> 00:46:40,744
Speaker 0: Those people who knew who they were responded correctly to the call-outs because they did the same set they've done forever.

543
00:46:40,985 --> 00:46:41,768
Speaker 0: Like no changes.

544
00:46:41,809 --> 00:46:43,454
Speaker 1: They don't, it's been 20 years.

545
00:46:43,494 --> 00:46:44,237
Speaker 1: They don't have new music.

546
00:46:44,257 --> 00:46:46,123
Speaker 0: We are the opening band.

547
00:46:46,144 --> 00:46:49,935
Speaker 0: It's literally like same everything, the pants song.

548
00:46:50,457 --> 00:46:55,191
Speaker 0: But I would say four fifths of that room had no idea what this was going to be.

549
00:46:55,773 --> 00:46:57,378
Speaker 0: And they were into it.

550
00:46:59,424 --> 00:46:59,986
Speaker 1: I mean, yeah.

551
00:47:00,086 --> 00:47:01,913
Speaker 1: You know, if you haven't seen it before, it works, right?

552
00:47:02,034 --> 00:47:04,769
Speaker 1: It's like, that's how Broadway show goes on for years and years and years.

553
00:47:04,789 --> 00:47:05,834
Speaker 1: It's like, yeah, this works.

554
00:47:06,316 --> 00:47:08,426
Speaker 1: And people haven't seen it until they've seen it.

555
00:47:08,547 --> 00:47:09,872
Speaker 1: It's you can't see it anywhere else.

556
00:47:09,892 --> 00:47:16,449
Speaker 1: You know, so I would say likely to have seen Paul storm or Jonathan Colton, unless you already knew who they were and sought them out.

557
00:47:17,833 --> 00:47:23,269
Speaker 0: So I would say having a concert at night at PAX Unplugged as an experiment was a huge success.

558
00:47:25,650 --> 00:47:28,684
Speaker 0: Panels got a ton of attendance across the board as far as I can tell.

559
00:47:28,744 --> 00:47:30,833
Speaker 0: Like our panel was at noon on Friday.

560
00:47:30,873 --> 00:47:35,411
Speaker 0: It was like the first thing, like the story time was like still going or just wrapping up.

561
00:47:35,471 --> 00:47:41,933
Speaker 0: Like it was, we were the first thing in that room and we were like a little of almost four fists of the way full.

562
00:47:42,194 --> 00:47:43,520
Speaker 0: I'd say in that room, I got a photo.

563
00:47:43,921 --> 00:47:44,685
Speaker 1: It's like a count.

564
00:47:45,488 --> 00:47:48,161
