00:55:18,318 --> 00:55:21,130
Speaker 1: Unplugged is good is until, until something changes.

675
00:55:24,692 --> 00:55:29,889
Speaker 0: Like magfest is limited basically primarily by the fact that there's no hotels anywhere near it.

676
00:55:31,111 --> 00:55:36,334
Speaker 1: But yeah, uh, I'm not so confident the video game industry is going to recover that quickly.

677
00:55:36,354 --> 00:55:44,189
Speaker 1: Uh, and I'm not going to say the tabletop will, will fall, but I'm not going to say that it's going to hold and keep growing forever.

678
00:55:44,710 --> 00:55:45,392
Speaker 1: It's good.

679
00:55:45,493 --> 00:55:46,556
Speaker 1: Eventually there's

680
00:55:46,596 --> 00:56:06,322
Speaker 0: a difference here is that if the video game industry falls, video game conventions all follow along with them for a lot of reasons, but tabletop, the demand from people who want tabletop conventions and want to play games is so much greater than even the money the industry makes.

681
00:56:06,964 --> 00:56:12,330
Speaker 0: that the community demand can almost make conventions happen even if the industry itself is not helping.

682
00:56:12,350 --> 00:56:17,192
Speaker 1: But then the badge price would have to make up for all the money they make from the expo hall instead.

683
00:56:17,212 --> 00:56:22,030
Speaker 1: And that would, that badge price might become prohibitive for the large tabletop.

684
00:56:22,151 --> 00:56:29,509
Speaker 0: While it might, my gut feeling, and this is pure gut feeling, if you doubled the price of a Pax Unplugged badge, I think it would still sell out.

685
00:56:30,650 --> 00:56:39,630
Speaker 1: Maybe if, but if there's no expo hall there because the industry flopped and people just want to play games that already exist, would people would be willing to pay twice as much for the con?

