689
00:56:50,287 --> 00:56:51,894
Speaker 0: So don't, read too much into this.

690
00:56:52,698 --> 00:56:57,842
Speaker 0: I really get the impression a lot of the people who were at Pax Unplugged were there for the whole weekend.

691
00:56:58,606 --> 00:56:59,490
Speaker 0: Like I'm here.

692
00:56:59,571 --> 00:57:02,270
Speaker 1: I do think there were more people who were there multiple days.

693
00:57:02,670 --> 00:57:08,368
Speaker 0: When Pax started, the original Paxes, they only sold badges for the whole weekend.

694
00:57:08,448 --> 00:57:13,021
Speaker 0: And old Pax West, only all weekend people were coming for the most part.

695
00:57:13,362 --> 00:57:15,308
Speaker 0: Pax East changed that.

696
00:57:15,749 --> 00:57:19,301
Speaker 0: That was when they shifted to selling individual day badges.

697
00:57:19,321 --> 00:57:24,901
Speaker 0: And I think that was the moment where Pax East suddenly like at night it cleared out.

698
00:57:24,962 --> 00:57:31,525
Speaker 0: because suddenly a huge percentage of the people who go to Pax East only come for one day and are primarily expo hall people.

699
00:57:31,986 --> 00:57:38,050
Speaker 0: Unplugged has resurfaced the old Pax culture of you come for the whole weekend.

700
00:57:40,990 --> 00:57:41,131
Speaker 1: Indeed.

701
00:57:41,212 --> 00:57:45,294
Speaker 1: Well, I mean, if you're, you know, you're looking to play games one day of games is not enough, right?

702
00:57:45,595 --> 00:57:49,269
Speaker 1: Also, you know, if you're coming to Unplugged, they're coming to play games.

703
00:57:49,330 --> 00:57:52,343
Speaker 1: If you go to East or West, people might not be coming to play games.

