722
00:58:43,763 --> 00:58:44,385
Speaker 1: Be quiet.

723
00:58:44,927 --> 00:58:47,818
Speaker 1: Stop talking games and all the stuff you did at Pax so badly.

724
00:58:47,838 --> 00:58:49,506
Speaker 1: There's only one quiet car.

725
00:58:49,526 --> 00:58:50,290
Speaker 1: I couldn't get in there.

726
00:58:51,750 --> 00:58:53,455
Speaker 1: They can't make all the cars quiet cars.

727
00:58:53,595 --> 00:58:55,621
Speaker 1: You can talk just quieter.

728
00:58:55,641 --> 00:58:57,205
Speaker 1: I'm old.

729
00:58:58,068 --> 00:58:58,329
Speaker 0: Yeah.

730
00:58:58,569 --> 00:59:00,740
Speaker 0: Younger, younger rim would have been more into that.

731
00:59:00,760 --> 00:59:02,248
Speaker 0: And that's why I am tolerant of it.

732
00:59:02,348 --> 00:59:05,904
Speaker 0: because uh, the old man should step aside.

733
00:59:06,045 --> 00:59:07,089
Speaker 0: Let the young man have fun.

734
00:59:08,151 --> 00:59:09,096
Speaker 1: They weren't that much younger.

735
00:59:09,116 --> 00:59:10,504
Speaker 1: These are, you know, twenties thirties.

736
00:59:10,604 --> 00:59:20,299
Speaker 0: That's a lot younger in terms of when I was in my twenties, they announced that Pax will no longer go until 2am and will in fact end at a cowardly midnight.

737
00:59:20,700 --> 00:59:22,365
Speaker 0: And I remember being mad about that.

738
00:59:22,365 --> 00:59:29,684
Speaker 0: 42 year old rim could not possibly make it to 2am out of Pax.

739
00:59:31,128 --> 00:59:31,630
Speaker 1: No, no chance.

740
00:59:35,592 --> 00:59:37,961
Speaker 0: This has been Geek Nights with Rim and Scott.

741
00:59:38,021 --> 00:59:40,591
Speaker 0: Special thanks to DJ Pretzel for the opening theme.

742
00:59:40,732 --> 00:59:46,795
Speaker 1: Be sure to visit our website at frontrowclue.com for show notes, discussion, links, and more.

743
00:59:47,237 --> 00:59:49,890
Speaker 0: Remember, Geek Nights is not one, but four different shows.

744
00:59:50,250 --> 00:59:51,877
Speaker 0: Mondays are science and technology.

745
00:59:51,917 --> 00:59:53,685
Speaker 0: Tuesdays gaming and games.

746
00:59:53,805 --> 00:59:55,613
Speaker 0: Wednesdays are animation and comics.

747
00:59:55,934 --> 00:59:58,464
Speaker 0: Thursdays are arbitrary and indiscriminate.

748
00:59:59,067 --> 01:00:04,044
Speaker 0: Geek Nights is distributed under a creative comments attribution 4.0 international license.

749
01:00:04,446 --> 01:00:12,732
Speaker 1: Geek Nights is recorded live with no studio and no audience, but unlike those other late shows, it's actually recorded at night.

750
01:00:13,355 --> 01:00:24,417
Speaker 0: And the Patreon patrons for this episode of Geek Nights are Alan Jones and PG Dredd, Lily Tenebrae, K-Spare, Mix of Music, Krista Voorhe, Clinton, Walt, and Finn, Joel Hayes, Penny Rhymer, Rebecca Adams, Sam Markey, Sandra Van Holl, and a bunch of people who do not want me to say their names.

751
01:00:24,659 --> 01:00:25,844
Speaker 0: Yeah, PAX Unplugged was great.

752
01:00:25,965 --> 01:00:28,995
Speaker 0: And for any of you who are wondering, zero trouble with the union.

753
01:00:29,457 --> 01:00:32,690
Speaker 0: One, the union guys were super cool and kind of into the content.

754
01:00:33,730 --> 01:00:50,892
Speaker 0: And two, the rules of the convention center, I actually learned them specifically, are you do not need to hire a camera operator, even if you have a tripod, as long as you do not plug into a power outlet and do not touch the camera or the tripod at any point during the event you're recording.

755
01:00:51,374 --> 01:00:53,803
Speaker 0: So we set up multiple cameras, no problem.

756
01:00:54,165 --> 01:00:57,037
Speaker 0: I'll try to have the panel up like this weekend at the latest.

757
01:00:57,579 --> 01:00:58,785
Speaker 0: So yeah, it was all a good time.

758
01:00:58,905 --> 01:01:00,651
Speaker 0: I hope to see you all at future PAX Unplugged.

759
01:01:01,031 --> 01:01:10,240
Speaker 0: And tonight I will leave you with... Hey Mario, look what I made.

760
01:01:10,840 --> 01:01:12,285
Speaker 0: It's a stone, Luigi.

761
01:01:12,586 --> 01:01:13,990
Speaker 0: You didn't make it.

762
01:01:15,535 --> 01:01:16,397
Speaker 0: It's a football.

763
01:01:16,678 --> 01:01:17,260
Speaker 0: I chiseled it.

764
01:01:17,780 --> 01:01:19,287
Speaker 0: Well, what are you waiting for?

765
01:01:19,668 --> 01:01:20,693
Speaker 1: Throw me a pass.

766
01:01:21,095 --> 01:01:22,240
Speaker 0: It's even official size.

767
01:01:24,169 --> 01:01:25,520
Speaker 1: But not official weight.

